#import "../template.typ": somatic_page

// PAGE 5: THE SOMATIC KEY
// Final introductory page before Phase 1 begins
// Deep scientific foundation + visual divider

#somatic_page(
  title: "The Shadow Lives in Your Body",
  body_text: [
    #rect(fill: rgb("#F5F5F0"), stroke: 0.5pt + gray, inset: 15pt, radius: 2pt)[
      Polyvagal theory teaches us that the body keeps score in ways the conscious mind cannot access. When a child is shamed for crying, the *event* may be forgotten, but the nervous system remembers—and tightens the throat every time vulnerability arises. When rage is punished, it does not vanish; it calcines into chronic tension in the jaw, the fists, the shoulders. The body becomes an archaeological site, layered with fossilized emotions waiting to be unearthed.
      
      This is the promise of *somatic shadow work*: you do not need to remember the story to release the holding pattern. The body speaks a language older than words. A sensation in the chest is not just a feeling—it is *data*. A tightening in the belly is not anxiety; it is your gut-brain signaling: *something here needs attention*.
      
      When you learn to translate these signals, you reclaim power. The shadow no longer hijacks you in moments of stress. Instead, it becomes a messenger, a guide, a collaborator in your own wholeness.
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    #align(center)[
      ◈ · ✦ · ◈
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    *Where the Shadow Hides in Your Body:*
    
    - *The Throat*: Silenced truth, unexpressed grief, swallowed words.
    - *The Chest/Heart*: Abandoned longing, unmetabolized loss, numbness.
    - *The Belly/Gut*: Shame, fear, the "knot" of chronic anxiety.
    - *The Jaw*: Suppressed anger, grinding self-restraint, protective vigilance.
    - *The Shoulders*: The weight of responsibility, armoring against the world.
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    As you move through this journal, you will be asked again and again: *"Where do you feel this?"* This is not metaphorical. It is cartographic. You are mapping the geography of your own soul.
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    #align(center)[
      _The work begins now._
    ]
  ],
  image_path: none,
  layout_style: "bottom"
)
